//! The binding roster: every name a deployment's configuration uses, in
//! one place.
//!
//! CLAUDE.md §7 forbids hand-maintained lists because they drift
//! silently, and this list had drifted into four homes before this
//! module existed: `sesame-worker`'s config parser, `wrangler.toml`,
//! `image/serve.mjs`, and `workerd/rig.ts`. A name added to one and
//! missed in another produces a deployment that boots and then refuses
//! at the first request that reads it, which is the worst place to find
//! out.
//!
//! This is the source, and `sesame-worker`'s config parser is held to it
//! mechanically: a test there scans its own source for `SESAME_*`
//! literals and asserts the two sets agree in both directions, so a name
//! rostered and never read fails, and a name read and never rostered
//! fails. The three configuration files are not yet held to it; holding
//! them is the deploy tooling's own job and lands with it.
//!
//! # Why the whole crate has no dependencies by default
//!
//! `sesame-worker` compiles to wasm and a dependency here is a
//! dependency in the bundle. Everything past the roster (the stage
//! grammar, the plan, the renders) sits behind the `plan` feature, which
//! only `sesame-cli` enables.

/// What a binding is, which decides where its value comes from and
/// whether it may ever be printed.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
pub enum BindingKind {
    /// A plain `[vars]` entry: a policy number, a URL, a word. Safe in a
    /// rendered config, a log, and a pull request.
    Var,
    /// A secret binding, pushed through `wrangler secret put` and never
    /// written to disk or rendered. Its value never leaves the operator's
    /// shell (CLAUDE.md §5).
    Secret,
    /// A platform binding rather than a value: a Hyperdrive connection,
    /// a send_email address. The deploy tooling wires it; no env carries
    /// it.
    Platform,
}

/// Whether a deployment must carry the binding.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
pub enum Requirement {
    /// Every deployment carries it, and config parse fails without it.
    Required,
    /// A deployment may omit it, and omitting it turns a surface off
    /// (ADR 0006's absent-config law).
    Optional,
    /// The grammar computes it from `(instance, stage)` and the origin,
    /// so an operator who sets it explicitly is overriding a derivation
    /// and the plan refuses.
    Derived,
}

/// One binding.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Binding {
    /// The name, spelled exactly as every home spells it.
    pub name: &'static str,
    /// Where its value comes from.
    pub kind: BindingKind,
    /// Whether a deployment must carry it.
    pub requirement: Requirement,
    /// One line an operator reads in the rendered variable table.
    pub summary: &'static str,
}

