//! The engine: a manifest and an instance in, an account converged.
//!
//! Two halves. The pure half ([`spec`], [`plan`], [`render`], [`diff`])
//! turns a manifest and an instance's facts into the exact requests the
//! Workers API takes, and the golden lane pins those bytes. The impure
//! half ([`apply`]) walks a sequence of idempotent steps against a
//! [`api::CloudflareApi`], reporting each as an event, and it is generic
//! over the trait so the lanes drive it against [`fake::FakeCloudflare`]
//! while the agent and the control plane drive it against the real API.
//!
//! Three properties the design leans on live here. Every step is
//! create-if-absent against a deterministic name, so a run interrupted
//! anywhere resumes by running again. Every worker the engine uploads
//! carries ownership tags, and pre-flight reads them, so a name collision
//! is classified rather than overwritten. And no secret's value ever
//! reaches a plan, an event, or an error: secrets are rendered into one
//! request body and nowhere else.

#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
#![allow(async_fn_in_trait)]

pub mod api;
pub mod apply;
pub mod diff;
pub mod plan;
pub mod render;
pub mod spec;

#[cfg(any(test, feature = "fake"))]
pub mod fake;

pub use apply::{Event, EventKind, Operation, Step};
pub use plan::Plan;
pub use spec::{InstanceSpec, Route};

